flowchart LR
    %% Scope discipline: in-scope claims (left) vs deliberate non-claims (right).

    subgraph IN["IN SCOPE — what this portfolio claims"]
        direction TB
        I1["Hub-spoke Azure landing zone<br/>Terraform + remote state + locking"]:::inscope
        I2["HA k3s cluster on Proxmox<br/>Ansible node-hardening role"]:::inscope
        I3["Matrix ApplicationSet<br/>N×M GitOps reconciliation"]:::inscope
        I4["LiteLLM/FastAPI gateway<br/>live, metrics exposed"]:::inscope
        I5["kube-prometheus-stack + Sealed Secrets<br/>runbook, restart test, key backup"]:::inscope
        I6["6 ADRs, 2 runbooks, 5 release tags<br/>incident response documented"]:::inscope
    end

    subgraph OUT["OUT OF SCOPE — deliberate non-claims"]
        direction TB
        O1["Multi-tenant production workload<br/>RBAC partitioning at scale"]:::outscope
        O2["AWS / GCP production depth<br/>(GCP on P6 roadmap, not built)"]:::outscope
        O3["Platform-team-of-N coordination<br/>(this is a one-architect portfolio)"]:::outscope
        O4["AKS currently running<br/>(torn down for £60 spend cap; rebuild = WU-5)"]:::outscope
        O5["Every WU closed<br/>(WU-3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 9 open and tracked)"]:::outscope
        O6["Formal 24/7 SRE on-call<br/>(MSP context, not in this repo)"]:::outscope
    end

    IN ~~~ OUT

    classDef inscope fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#166534,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#0f172a;
